import json,re
from pathlib import Path
r=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
a=json.loads((r/'data/flows.json').read_text())
sources={
'headspace':('Headspace · Sleep','https://www.headspace.com/content/categories/sleep','Sleepcasts, music, soundscapes and wind-down content support separate ritual and audio destinations. The specific routine, timer and navigation below are WDA proposals.'),
'planta':('Planta','https://getplanta.com/','Plant care, plant collections and journals inform a plant-centered structure. The painterly presentation remains Pocket Garden’s original direction.'),
'planta-start':('Planta · Getting started','https://getplanta.com/discover/getstartedwithplanta','Adding plants to sites, completing or postponing tasks, and keeping plant notes inform setup → garden → care → observation.'),
'planta-care':('Planta · Custom care','https://getplanta.com/discover/iam/custom/care','Custom tasks can have descriptions and recurrence. Pocket Garden uses an observation before recording care; it does not assume every reminder requires watering.'),
'cozi':('Cozi · Feature overview','https://www.cozi.com/feature-overview/','Shared calendars, reminders and lists support a household agenda. Home Note’s invitation, acknowledgement and handover details are proposed here, not copied native flows.'),
'weather':('Apple · Check the weather','https://support.apple.com/guide/iphone/check-the-weather-iph1ac0b35f/ios','Current conditions and forecast detail support a summary-to-detail hierarchy. Soul’s city, preferences and daylight routes are WDA design decisions.'),
'hue':('I Love Hue · Official product page','https://zutgames.com/i-love-hue.php','Calm visual arrangement informs the play loop. Horizontal botanical strips, snapping rules and tap alternatives are Petal-specific proposals.'),
'structured':('Structured','https://structured.app/','A visual timeline and calendar integration inform Daybook’s planning structure. Its daylight landscape and saved places remain original to this study.'),
'structured-tasks':('Structured · Create and edit tasks','https://help.structured.app/en/articles/338050','Task creation, date/time/duration editing and saving back into the timeline support an explicit editor. Daybook additionally preserves drafts and derives the duration from start/end.'),
'onboarding':('Apple · Onboarding','https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/onboarding','Reference retained from the research plan. Full article could not be read through the text fetch, so no specific behavior is attributed to it. The proposed short setup sequences are WDA decisions.'),
'forms':('W3C · Validating input','https://www.w3.org/WAI/tutorials/forms/validation/','Label required fields and expose accessible validation feedback. Validate on the server as well as the client. Failed saves should keep the user’s draft.'),
'dialog':('W3C · Modal dialog pattern','https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/dialog-modal/','Modal focus stays inside the dialog; Escape closes it. Restore useful focus on return. Dirty drafts require an explicit discard choice.'),
'drag':('W3C · Dragging movements','https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/dragging-movements.html','Provide a single-pointer alternative to dragging. Petal uses tap a strip, then its target, with keyboard support in addition.'),
 'tabs':('W3C · Tabs pattern','https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/tabs/','In-page tabs need matching panels and keyboard behavior. The study’s bottom destinations are route navigation: implement links with aria-current, rather than applying tab semantics to unrelated pages.'),
'motion':('MDN · Reduced motion','https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@media/prefers-reduced-motion','Respect the system’s request to reduce nonessential movement. Motion is never the only signal that an action succeeded.'),
'permission':('MDN · Notification permission','https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Notification/requestPermission_static','Permission can be granted, denied or undecided. Keep reminder state separate from requested permission and retain a usable path after refusal.')}
(r/'research/sources.json').write_text(json.dumps({k:dict(title=v[0],url=v[1],finding=v[2],checked='2026-10-21',access='partial' if k=='onboarding' else 'read') for k,v in sources.items()},indent=2)+'\n')
aux={
'sign-in':'Email/sign-in method → explicit Continue → loading → restore account after success. Invalid credentials show an inline error. Cancel returns to welcome; never replace local data before a merge decision.',
'settings':'Show preference rows and account/help links in a sheet. Each switch exposes its actual saved value. Close returns to the invoking tab, scroll and focus; notification permission remains a separate explicit action.',
'notification-permission':'Explain the specific reminder; Continue invokes the platform prompt. Granted enables and schedules; denied or dismissed keeps reminders off with a Settings/help route. Cancel returns to the exact invoking control. Do not prompt on every visit.',
'ritual-player':'Show selected ritual title, duration and remaining time; Start is explicit. Pause retains elapsed time, Resume continues; End asks whether to end early. Only a completed ritual sets its completion flag. Return to the source tab with the same ritual selected.',
'sleep-timer':'Offer Off / 10 / 20 / 30 minutes plus Cancel. Apply stores timer end independently of audio track length; expiry pauses audio and announces finished. The pictured 20-minute track has 15 minutes of audio remaining.',
'plant-search':'Search species with a labeled input, loading, no-results and retry states. Choose a result or Unknown; apply the species ID to the plant draft. Cancel preserves the previous value.',
'plant-detail':'Show Pip’s name, species, location, observation history and Edit. Edit uses the plant form with the same record ID; saving updates rather than creates. Back restores the source screen.',
'snooze':'Choose later today, tomorrow or a date/time; Apply changes the task due time, not its completion status. Cancel preserves the old date. Reminder permission refusal does not prevent saving a new due time.',
'plant-picker':'List known plants with the current selection. Selecting a different plant confirms reassigning a dirty note, then returns to the same draft. Cancel keeps Pip and all entered text.',
'photo-picker':'Open the platform’s limited photo picker only on Add a photo. Selection shows a removable thumbnail and upload progress. Cancel changes nothing; failed upload retains the note and allows retry/removal before saving.',
'discard-note':'Keep editing returns focus to the draft. Discard clears only the unsaved note and returns to the Notes list; it never deletes a saved observation.',
'join-household':'Enter invitation code/link → validate → show household and inviter → Accept. Expired/revoked codes show retry/help. Accept joins exactly that household; cancel leaves membership unchanged.',
'account':'Show current person and household, profile edit and preferences. Save validates the display name and updates the same person ID. Close returns to Today; switching household requires a separate explicit choice.',
'handover-detail':'Show selected time, item, assignee and notes. Owner can Edit; other roles see the permitted actions. Save updates the same item with conflict handling; Back leaves the agenda unchanged.',
'note-editor':'Labeled title/body with Save and Cancel. New notes start blank; edit loads the selected note ID. Required title (1–80) and body (1–2000); Save prevents duplicate submits. Cancel offers Keep editing / Discard if dirty.',
'person-detail':'Show Avery, Owner and permitted contact/profile fields. No automatic messaging. Close returns to People. Destructive membership changes require authorization and confirmation.',
'invite-detail':'Show Morgan, pending status and sent timestamp, plus Resend and Cancel invitation. Pending is not membership. Close preserves the list; revoked or accepted state refreshes visibly.',
'cancel-invite':'Confirm revoking Morgan’s pending invitation with Keep invitation / Cancel invitation. A successful request reduces pending count to zero; failure retains the invitation and offers retry.',
'invite-form':'Enter recipient and optional display name → Review recipient and household → Send invitation. Sending is explicit. Success adds one pending row, failure keeps the form. Cancel sends nothing.',
'location-permission':'Use my location explains foreground lookup, then requests it on Continue. Resolve coordinates to a named city with confirmation. Denial, timeout or unavailable result returns to manual search; never invent a location.',
'city-search':'Labeled city search, clear-query button, result list with country and timezone, loading/no-results/error states. Selection uses a stable city ID. Add/Use is explicit; duplicate saved city selects the existing record. Cancel restores the invoking route and draft.',
'hour-detail':'Present the chosen hour, temperature and available forecast metrics with a data timestamp. Previous/Next hour controls and an accessible text table are alternatives to the chart. Missing data uses a dash and explanation, not zero.',
'weather-detail':'Show the selected metric, units, explanation and provider timestamp; keep missing/error values distinct. Close returns focus to Wind or Humidity, not the top of the page.',
'daylight-detail':'Show sunrise, sunset and daylight window as readable times with timezone/source. Optional reminder requires its own explicit action. Close returns to the initiating row/arc; polar-day/no-data states need explanatory text.',
'manage-city':'An accessible More menu exposes Move up/down and Remove. Swipe may reveal the same actions but is never required. Removal offers Undo; removing the active/home city first selects another or returns to setup if none remain.',
'location-preference':'Offer Manual city and Current location. Manual opens saved/search cities. Choosing Current requests permission only if needed; denial retains Manual and the previously saved city.',
'legal-and-sources':'Readable Privacy and Data sources documents with heading, links, provider attribution and Close/Back. Preserve Settings scroll; external links are identified and do not silently change the current preference.',
'restore-progress':'Offer Continue on this device and optional sign-in restore. Show local and remote counts before an explicit merge; union completed IDs without adding duplicates. Cancel keeps guest progress.',
'pause':'Modal with Resume, Restart and Collections. Resume restores offsets, Restart opens its confirmation, Collections saves partial state. Escape/Back resumes; focus returns to the selected strip.',
'restart-confirm':'Keep playing preserves every strip offset. Restart resets only the current puzzle’s in-progress arrangement, never the completed-ID history or other collections.',
'account-link':'Optional account linking with consent to sync local progress. Success unions puzzle IDs; failure retains all guest data and offers retry. Cancel returns to Profile without a lost-progress warning loop.',
'calendar-permission':'Explain read-only calendar import → select provider/calendar → explicit Connect. Show loading and connected status only after success. Denied, cancelled or unavailable returns to manual planning. Imported items keep source IDs; editing read-only events opens the source or creates an explicitly separate local copy.',
'date-picker':'Labeled month/year and date grid, previous/next month and Today. Keyboard date navigation and typed-date alternative. Apply selects day in Europe/Lisbon; Cancel preserves date and scroll.',
'plan-editor':'Use the plan editor for the selected record, including dinner; it carries recordId and returnTo. Save updates that record only. Cancel preserves saved values; errors keep the draft.',
'discard-plan':'Keep editing returns to the dirty form. Discard restores the saved 18:30–19:05 / 35-minute walk and returns to the caller. Never commit the displayed 40-minute draft implicitly.',
'delete-plan':'Confirm Delete / Keep plan. Success removes the selected record and returns to Today with Undo; failure keeps the form and record. Undo restores the original ID and times.',
'place-detail':'Show saved name, description and location with Edit and Use in a plan. In editor-picker mode, Select this place returns its ID to the existing draft. Back never discards that draft.',
'place-editor':'Labeled name (1–80), note (0–500), city/location, Save and Cancel. Create increments saved count once; edit updates the same ID. Duplicate candidates offer Use existing / Keep separate. Dirty Cancel confirms discard.'}
kind={
'button':('Tap/click; Enter or Space','Button with visible focus; pending state only for asynchronous work. Return focus after a sheet closes.'),
'link':('Tap/click; Enter','Route link; announce destination heading after navigation and restore scroll on Back.'),
'submit':('Tap/click or form Enter','Validate, focus first invalid field, preserve draft; disable duplicate submission while pending. Success commits once; failure offers Retry.'),
'input':('Focus, type; blur validates','Native labeled input; errors use aria-describedby and aria-invalid. Keyboard must not cover the active field.'),
'combobox':('Type/search then select','Accessible combobox/listbox, clear action, arrow navigation, Enter select, Escape close. Distinguish query from selected record ID.'),
'textarea':('Focus/type; multiline Enter','Labeled textarea; preserve line breaks, character limit and draft. Save is a separate explicit action.'),
'radio':('Tap option; arrow keys','Native radio group with one selection and a visible legend; selected and focus states are distinct.'),
'switch':('Tap or Space','Native checkbox styled as switch; label and checked state agree. Permission-dependent value stays off until granted.'),
'time':('Tap/scroll picker or type','Native time input/numeric alternative; 24-hour storage with localized display. Validate and derive related labels from one value.'),
'date':('Tap picker or type','Calendar with keyboard support and typed alternative; keep timezone explicit. Selected date is not keyboard focus.'),
'select':('Tap then choose; keyboard','Labeled select; preserve old value on Cancel and announce the chosen value.'),
'range':('Tap track, drag or arrow keys','Native range with min/max and human-readable elapsed/remaining labels; clamp bounds and support larger keyboard steps.'),
'chart':('Tap point; keyboard move','Each data point has an accessible label; text table duplicates data. Pointer hover may preview but does not hide essential information.'),
'puzzle':('Drag, tap-select/tap-target, or keys','Pointer capture only after drag intent; vertical scroll remains available. Snap from real positions and announce aligned count. Escape cancels a move.'),
'option':('Tap/click or Enter','Listbox option with aria-selected; selecting updates the draft record ID and visible label.'),
'context':('More button; optional swipe','Explicit menu button with expanded state and keyboard navigation. Swipe reveals equivalent actions; it never performs deletion immediately.'),
'event':('State transition','Not a visible button. Derived condition fires once per record, persists idempotently and announces the new state.'),
'status':('No input','Noninteractive text/status; polite live region only for changes, no focus move or clickable affordance.')}
alternatives={
'afterglow':('Routine first','An alternative welcome can offer a two-minute breathing preview before asking for a time. On finishing, offer Save this rhythm or Continue without reminders. Compare first-session completion and time-to-first-ritual; keep guest use available.'),
'pocket-garden':('Sample garden first','Let visitors explore an explicitly labeled demo before adding a plant. Demo care and notes remain in a separate namespace; Create my garden opens an empty plant form. Compare setup completion and accidental demo-record saves.'),
'home-note':('Invitation first','For households arriving from an invitation link, show the household and inviter before account/setup. Accept joins; creating a new household remains secondary. Compare failed joins and duplicate households.'),
'soul':('Manual city first','Default to city search. Offer location only as a secondary explicit shortcut and move reminder setup until after the first forecast. Compare first forecast success, permission denial recovery and city corrections.'),
'petal':('Play before library','Try a little arrangement can lead directly to Citrus 01; completing it opens the library with 1/12. Keep tutorial progress separate. Compare first puzzle completion and ability to find another collection.'),
'daybook':('Plan before calendar','Start with one local evening plan, then offer read-only calendar import after saving. Manual planning remains complete on its own. Compare first-plan save and duplicate imported events.')}
checks={
'afterglow':['2 + 5 + 8 = 15 minutes; routine runs 22:30–22:45.','Library membership and Tonight derive from the same routine IDs; no duplicate entries.','Sound image is a later playing state after explicit Play: 05:00 + 15:00 = 20:00. Opening Sounds alone is paused.','Editing a saved time returns to Tonight; Back in edit mode does not reopen welcome.'],
'pocket-garden':['Create Pip once; duplicate taps/retry keep one record.','Still damp saves an observation, never a watering event.','After Save soil check the due count becomes zero; Undo restores the task.','Save note replaces the editor with one dated note; Cancel never deletes earlier notes.'],
'home-note':['Friday 19 June 2026 is the fixture date; it is not live device data.','Setup creates Avery only. Screen 05 is reached after an explicitly sent Morgan invitation.','One member plus one pending invite is not two members.','Read acknowledgement requires Mark read; merely expanding a note does not acknowledge it.'],
'soul':['Six hourly values match six timestamps and chart direction.','Porto/Faro are suggestions until Add; saving one yields two saved cities.','Permission denied retains manual Lisbon and keeps reminders off.','Unit changes reformat all values from canonical data, including feels-like and wind.'],
'petal':['Play contains five strips; 1, 3 and 5 aligned = 3/5 = 60%.','Completion aligns all five and stores Citrus 01 exactly once.','Collections pictured before play is 0/12; after completion it becomes 1/12.','Profile total counts completed IDs, not visits; replay cannot inflate the count.'],
'daybook':['At 18:00, sunset 20:58 leaves 2h 58m.','Before edit, walk 18:30–19:05 = 35 minutes; draft end 19:10 = 40.','Save commits 40 minutes; Cancel keeps 35. Reminder 10 minutes before 18:30 is 18:20.','Week is 15–21 June 2026; Thursday is 18 June. Preserve Europe/Lisbon.']}
for app in a:
 app['alternatives']=[{'title':alternatives[app['id']][0],'detail':alternatives[app['id']][1]}]
 app['checks']=checks[app['id']]
 app['auxiliary_routes']={k:aux[k] for k in sorted({c['target'][4:] for s in app['screens'] for c in s['controls'] if c['target'].startswith('aux:')})}
 for s in app['screens']:
  for c in s['controls']:
   c['trigger'],c['implementation']=kind[c['kind']]
  s['shared_controls']=[]
  if s['selected_tab']:
   for i,(label,target) in enumerate(zip(app['tabs'],app['tab_routes'])):
    s['shared_controls'].append({'id':f"{app['id']}.{s['number']:02d}.nav.{i+1}",'label':label,'kind':'navigation','target':target,'trigger':'Tap/click or Enter','effect':f"Open {label}; show only its selected state. Preserve independent tab scroll and draft state; selecting the active destination is a no-op.",'implementation':'Route link inside nav; aria-current=page on the active destination. No automatic save, sound or permission request on navigation.'})
  s['display_notes']='Brand, headings, body copy, background texture, decorative vignettes and dividers are noninteractive. Read meaningful copy in document order; decorative artwork uses empty alt. OS chrome is intentionally omitted from exports; production safe-area insets belong to the app shell. Step markers communicate progress and are not buttons. Numeric totals derive from saved data or the explicitly described draft. Any exceptions appear in the control ledger.'
  s['scroll_notes']='One vertical scroll region. Preserve the airy spacing; at small heights or large text allow scrolling instead of scaling text down. Keep the bottom destination navigation above the safe area when present, and add content inset so it covers nothing. Keyboard opening scrolls the focused field into view; closing it restores the prior position. No horizontal paging gesture changes destination.'
  s['hover_notes']='Touch is primary. Fine-pointer hover may tint or underline an existing control in 120 ms, with an equivalent focus-visible state. It never reveals the only way to act. Press feedback uses opacity/color, no layout shift. Default route transition is a 160 ms crossfade; honor reduced motion with an immediate change. Botanical and weather artwork is still by default.'
(r/'data/flows.json').write_text(json.dumps(a,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)+'\n')
(r/'interaction').mkdir(exist_ok=True)
for app in a:
 md=f"# {app['name']} — flow and interaction review\n\nJason Festa / WDA · 21 October 2026\n\nFive visual states, with additional routes specified below. These are proposed product behaviors for later implementation; the review images are not functional app screens.\n\n## Direction\n\n{app['decision']}\n\n{app['style']}\n\nType: {', '.join(app['fonts'])}. Palette: {', '.join(app['palette'])}.\n\n## Reference chain\n\nOriginal art direction: [saved screen](../references/originals/{app['original']}.png). [Original prompt](../prompts/{app['original']}.txt). Historical research: [mobile research](../research/archive/mobile-research-2026-10-20.md), [state plan](../research/archive/mobile-state-plan-2026-10-20.md), [expanded flow research](../research/archive/expanded-flow-research-2026-10-20.md).\n\nCurrent product and interaction references were checked on 21 October 2026. Product documentation establishes features, not a hands-on audit of each native screen.\n\n"
 for key in app['sources']:
  t,u,f=sources[key]; md+=f"- [{t}]({u}) — {f}\n"
 md+='\n## Action flow\n\n'+ ' → '.join(f"{s['number']:02d} {s['title']}" for s in app['screens'])+'\n\nThe sequence shows representative states, not five mandatory steps on every visit. Returning users land on the last valid main destination; completed onboarding is skipped. Tab routes remain available independently of this reading order.\n\n'
 md+='| Destination | Route | Return rule |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n'
 for lab,target in zip(app['tabs'],app['tab_routes']):md+=f'| {lab} | `{target}` | Preserve its scroll, selection and draft; active destination does not reload. |\n'
 md+=f"\n## Fixed review data\n\n{app['fixture']}\n\n"+'\n'.join('- '+x for x in app['checks'])+'\n'
 for s in app['screens']:
  md+=f"\n## {s['number']:02d} · {s['title']}\n\nEntry: {s['entry']}. Selected destination: {s['selected_tab'] or 'none; setup or full-screen editor'}.\n\n[Screen image](../{s['image']}) · [Exact prompt](../{s['prompt']})\n\nPictured state: {s['visual']}\n\n### Control ledger\n\n| ID / element | Input | Result and route | React / accessibility |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n"
  for c in s['controls']+s['shared_controls']:
   md+=f"| `{c['id']}` · {c['label']} | {c['trigger']} | {c['effect']} Route: `{c['target']}`. | {c['implementation']} |\n"
  md+=f"\n### Display, scroll and hover\n\n{s['display_notes']}\n\n{s['scroll_notes']}\n\n{s['hover_notes']}\n"
 md+='\n## Additional routes and recovery\n\nThese states are specified, not additional image exports. Every `aux:` destination in the ledger is defined here. Shared loading, error, back and persistence behavior is in the [React handoff](react-handoff.md).\n\n'
 for k,v in app['auxiliary_routes'].items():md+=f'### {k}\n\n{v}\n\n'
 md+=f"## Alternative to evaluate\n\n**{app['alternatives'][0]['title']}.** {app['alternatives'][0]['detail']}\n\n## Implementation acceptance\n\n- Every visible control maps to a ledger ID; decorative and operating-system content is explicitly excluded.\n- Resolve every route and carry `returnTo`, record ID and draft ID through editors.\n- Test primary flow plus back/cancel, rejected permission, empty data, failed save/retry, offline resume and duplicate activation.\n- Test keyboard-only, screen reader order, reduced motion, 200% text and a narrow viewport; no clipped controls or hidden essential actions.\n- Verify the fixed data checks above with shared selectors rather than hardcoded repeated strings.\n"
 (r/f'interaction/{app["id"]}.md').write_text(md)
(r/'research/README.md').write_text('# App study — research package\n\nJason Festa / WDA · 21 October 2026\n\nThe six original screens establish art direction. Saved WDA research establishes the product categories and earlier flow thinking. Current official product pages and interaction guidance inform the proposed behaviors. No competitor screen is claimed to be a verified live native flow. Mobbin flow search was unavailable because the connected service requires a paid plan; no results from that search are used.\n\n## Saved research\n\n- [Mobile research](archive/mobile-research-2026-10-20.md)\n- [Earlier state matrix](archive/mobile-state-plan-2026-10-20.md)\n- [Expanded research](archive/expanded-flow-research-2026-10-20.md)\n\n## Current source findings\n\n'+'\n\n'.join(f'### {v[0]}\n\n[Primary source]({v[1]}). Checked 21 October 2026.\n\n{v[2]}' for v in sources.values())+'\n\n## Application to this study\n\n'+ '\n'.join(f'- [{x["name"]} flow and control ledger](../interaction/{x["id"]}.md)' for x in a)+'\n\nAll detailed app routes, copy, fixtures and motion timings are proposed WDA decisions. Alternative routes are documented for comparison; they are not additional exported screens.\n')
print('Wrote six interaction ledgers and research index')
